  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "1. Dissolve ingredients except bicarbonate, yeast extract, vitamins and sulfide, then sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials to 30% of their volume and autoclave."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "Add yeast extract, vitamins (sterilized by filtration) and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas atmosphere and bicarbonate from a sterile anoxic stock solution prepared under 80% N2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "Neutralize the sodium sulfide with sterile H2SO4 (see medium 29). After completing the medium adjust pH to 6.8-7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "2. Inoculated vessels are pressurized with sterile carbon monoxide gas to 2 bar overpressure."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "Dissolve EDTA in 800 ml distilled water, adjust pH to 7 using 2 N NaOH and add ferrous chloride."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "After ferrous chloride has dissolved add other compounds. Finally adjust pH to 6.0 and bring volume to 1000 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": "The sulfide solution is prepared in a 250 ml screw-capped bottle with a butyl rubber septum and a magnetic stirrer."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": "The solution is bubbled with nitrogen gas, closed and autoclaved for 15 min. at 121°C"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 19,
      "comment": "After cooling to room temperature the pH is adjusted to about 7.0 by adding of sterile 2 M H2SO4 drop-wise with a syringe without opening the bottle."
    }
  ]
}